<<<
lather, The OED gives only lă- (rhyming with gather, not father); & an obsolete spelling ladder shows the old vowel sound. Though lah’dher is often heard, l. apparently does not belong to the class of words in which ah & ă are merely southern & northern variants (pass &c.).
===
**lather.** The OED gives only lă- (rhyming with *gather*, not *father*); & an obsolete spelling *ladder* shows the old vowel sound. Though lah'dh*er* is often heard, *l.* apparently does not belong to the class of words in which ah & ă are merely southern & northern variants (*pass* &c.).
>>>

